# HOOHR - line endings are load-bearing, not cosmetic.
#
# The biggest offender is docker/entrypoint.sh. A Windows clone defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF; a CRLF shell script fails
# inside the container with a bare `\r: command not found`, and since the
# entrypoint is what migrates and seeds, that means "no database, no admin
# account, no app" - on precisely the machine we are trying to support.
#
# The .ps1 files are additionally saved as UTF-8 *with* a BOM. Git preserves
# the BOM (it is ordinary content, not a line ending), and PowerShell 5.1 -
# the version Windows ships - decodes a BOM-less UTF-8 file as the system ANSI
# codepage, turning every Korean character into mojibake. Keep the BOM if you
# edit them: re-save as UTF-8 with BOM, not "UTF-8".

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
